# NOCA -- Auto-Limit profiling caps
#
# The one profiling number two modules need for different reasons: the autojudge
# enforces it on every reference-implementation run, and the Web Limits tab
# states it up front so an author knows what will make a profiling run fail
# before spending one. A value in two templates drifts, and the half that drifts
# is the half nobody is looking at -- so it lives here, in the layer whose
# readers are exactly those two.
#
# Loaded by: autojudge, web
# Reference: docs/CONFIG.md -- layer map: docs/ENV_LAYERS.md

# Hard CPU-time ceiling for a *single* profiling execution. A test case of N
# repetitions gets N times this in aggregate, and no one run may exceed this.
NOCA_JUDGE_PROFILING_MAX_CPU_TIME_SEC=10.0
